**Definition 5.3 (one exact joint support).** For each resulting case $\tau$,
let $\mathbf p$ contain every finite-mode original rank and every fresh finite
index, including inversion indices. Let $\mathbf w$ contain the finite
values of every divergent original rank, including invisible coordinates.
Put all preliminary, inversion and image conditions in $\Gamma_\tau$.
Fix exactly the canonically finite original residuals $f_i(\mathbf p)$ of
Theorem 4.4; the other original chart residuals remain unrestricted finite
variables for the signed feasibility computation.

[SFS, Lemma 5.1][SFS] gives the exact Presburger predicate
$\Psi_{r,\tau}(\mathbf p,\mathbf w)$ for simultaneous feasibility of that
chart's entire negative list at these fixed finite values. Restore the
original rank incidence by $\mathbf n_r(\mathbf p,\mathbf w)$ and put

$$
\begin{aligned}
\Phi_\tau(\mathbf p,\mathbf w)
 &=\Gamma_\tau(\mathbf p)\ \land\
 \bigwedge_{r\in B}
 \left(P_{r,b_r}(\mathbf n_r(\mathbf p,\mathbf w))
       \land\Psi_{r,\tau}(\mathbf p,\mathbf w)\right),\\
G_\tau
 &=\{\mathbf p:\forall M\in\mathbb N\ \exists\mathbf w\
 [\Phi_\tau(\mathbf p,\mathbf w)\land
       \bigwedge_{j\ {\rm divergent}} w_j\ge M]\}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{NIS.17}
$$

This is one joint support, with every original sharing and correlation.
Empty products have their singleton meaning. Finite parameters are chosen
before all depth requirements. Neither
$\forall M\exists\mathbf p,\mathbf w$ nor separate cofinal marginals
substitutes for (NIS.17).

